WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.116
Keys help us answer a basic question

00:00:02.432 --> 00:00:05.843
which row are we talking about A

00:00:05.857 --> 00:00:08.396
primary key is the official row identifier

00:00:08.422 --> 00:00:11.372
selected for a table A natural key

00:00:11.399 --> 00:00:13.464
comes from the business domain such as

00:00:13.491 --> 00:00:15.951
a medical record number or national provider

00:00:15.978 --> 00:00:20.306
identifier A surrogate key is generated by

00:00:20.319 --> 00:00:22.424
the database and has no business meaning

00:00:23.361 --> 00:00:26.085
An alternate key is another candidate identifier

00:00:26.111 --> 00:00:27.953
that still needs uniqueness even though it

00:00:27.966 --> 00:00:31.873
is not the primary key A composite

00:00:31.899 --> 00:00:35.454
key uses several columns together A foreign

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:37.665
key references a key in another table

00:00:39.407 --> 00:00:40.999
Do not think of all keys as

00:00:41.025 --> 00:00:45.725
interchangeable They solve different problems
identity business

00:00:45.751 --> 00:00:50.565
uniqueness and relationships As we continue pay

00:00:50.592 --> 00:00:52.408
attention to which key is being used

00:00:52.434 --> 00:00:53.342
for each purpose
